---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import capture from '../../../../docs/media/recorded-terminal.jpg';
import Claim from '../../components/Claim.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import { descriptions, markFiles, palette, wordCount } from '../../data/brand.ts';
import { repository, sourceUrl } from '../../data/labels.ts';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Brand and press kit — Boardroom"
  description="The BOARDROOM mark, palette, typography, a real terminal capture and ready-to-use descriptions, with the rules for using them."
  eyebrow="Brand"
  heading="Brand and press kit"
  lede="Everything you need to write about Boardroom or link to it: the mark, the palette, the typefaces, a real capture of the product and two descriptions that say what exists today."
  wide
>
  <section aria-labelledby="mark-title">
    <h2 id="mark-title">The mark</h2>
    <p>
      A table seen from above: three advisers around it, and you, highlighted, in the seat that decides. The number of
      advisers is not a limit; the room is yours to compose.
    </p>
    <ul class="marks">
      {markFiles.map(mark => (
        <li class:list={['mark-card', mark.theme]}>
          <img src={`/brand/${mark.file}`} alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" />
          <p>{mark.label}</p>
          <a download href={`/brand/${mark.file}`}>Download SVG<span class="visually-hidden">: {mark.label}</span></a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <h3>Wordmark</h3>
    <p class="wordmark-sample"><Mark size={32} /><span>Boardroom</span></p>
    <p>
      The wordmark is the mark followed by the name set in Inter SemiBold, uppercase, tracked at 0.22 em. In running text,
      write <strong>Boardroom</strong>; <strong>BOARDROOM</strong> is used in the repository and technical documents.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="palette-title">
    <h2 id="palette-title">Palette</h2>
    <p>“The room at night”: deep blue-green surfaces, paper-coloured text and one lamp-lit accent. Every pair meets WCAG 2.2 AA in both themes.</p>
    <ul class="swatches">
      {palette.map(color => (
        <li class="swatch" data-swatch={color.token}>
          <span class="chips" aria-hidden="true">
            <span style={`background:${color.dark}`}></span>
            <span style={`background:${color.light}`}></span>
          </span>
          <strong>{color.name}</strong>
          <span class="role">{color.role}</span>
          <code>Dark {color.dark}</code>
          <code>Light {color.light}</code>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="type-title">
    <h2 id="type-title">Typography</h2>
    <ul class="type">
      <li><span class="sample display">Great decisions deserve a room.</span><span>Instrument Serif — display headings. SIL Open Font License 1.1.</span></li>
      <li><span class="sample sans">Your models. Your experts. Your ambition.</span><span>Inter — text and interface. SIL Open Font License 1.1.</span></li>
      <li><span class="sample mono">boardroom demo --data-dir ./example</span><span>The reader's own monospace font — terminal and code.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="capture-title">
    <h2 id="capture-title">A real capture</h2>
    <figure>
      <Image src={capture} alt="Boardroom recorded example in a real terminal: a proposal, two objections citing context.md, a revised proposal, and final views with two approvals and one insufficient-evidence verdict; the human decision is pending." widths={[640, 969]} sizes="(max-width: 64rem) 100vw, 969px" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>
        The packaged application in a real Windows pseudoterminal, playing the recorded example — a scripted, fictional
        meeting. The frame is added; no terminal line is rewritten. <a href={sourceUrl('docs/media/README.md')} rel="noopener">Provenance</a> ·
        <a href={sourceUrl('docs/media/recorded-example.cast')} rel="noopener">Raw recording</a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="descriptions-title">
    <h2 id="descriptions-title">Descriptions</h2>
    <div class="descriptions">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Short · {wordCount(descriptions.short)} words</h3>
        <p data-description="short">{descriptions.short}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Long · {wordCount(descriptions.long)} words</h3>
        <p data-description="long">{descriptions.long}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Claim id="open-source-license" />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="rules-title">
    <h2 id="rules-title">Using the brand</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep the mark's proportions and colours; use the version that matches your background.</li>
      <li>Always present the recorded example as a scripted, fictional meeting. The live workflow is implemented; real-account qualification for Plan 02 remains pending.</li>
      <li>Verdict colours never stand alone: show the words Approved, Rejected or Insufficient evidence with them.</li>
      <li>Do not suggest an endorsement, a partnership or usage figures. Boardroom publishes none.</li>
      <li>For anything else, <a href={`${repository}/issues/new`} rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Current limits are listed on the <a href="/engineering/#limits-title">engineering page</a> and the next steps on the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .marks,
  .swatches,
  .type {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .marks {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(12rem, 1fr));
  }

  .mark-card {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--surface-1);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .mark-card img {
    padding: var(--space-3);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
  }

  .mark-card.dark img {
    background: #101924;
  }

  .mark-card.light img {
    background: #f5f4ec;
  }

  .wordmark-sample {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--text-strong);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .swatches {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
  }

  .swatch {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--surface-1);
  }

  .chips {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    height: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
  }

  .swatch strong {
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .role {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .swatch code {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .type li {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .sample {
    color: var(--text-strong);
  }

  .sample.display {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .sample.sans {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .sample.mono {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  figure {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin: 0;
  }

  figure :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 969px;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
  }

  figcaption {
    max-width: 46rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .descriptions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .descriptions .panel {
    align-content: start;
  }

  .descriptions h3 {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>
